WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:13.849
It a busy day at Metro City Central Bank.

2
00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:18.934
"I need some money," a customer said.

3
00:00:20.255 --> 00:00:21.736
The bank teller typed on a computer.

4
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:23.818
A drawer popped open.

5
00:00:23.838 --> 00:00:27.240
"Uh-oh," the bank teller said.

6
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.622
"There's no more money in the drawer.

7
00:00:30.923 --> 00:00:31.324
Wait here.

8
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.721
I'll get it from the safe."

9
00:00:34.823 --> 00:00:37.385
He went over to the safe, unlocked the door, and opened it.

10
00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:39.587
The bank teller gasped.

11
00:00:39.607 --> 00:00:43.430
"All the money is gone!"

12
00:00:44.691 --> 00:00:47.193
"Wow!" Mara said.

13
00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.915
"Saturn's rings are amazing."

14
00:00:50.896 --> 00:00:53.158
Roxy and her friends were in the computer center at school.

15
00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:55.960
They were doing research projects for science.

16
00:00:56.981 --> 00:00:59.964
"I'd like to run around Saturn on its rings," Jack said.

17
00:01:01.212 --> 00:01:02.233
Mara rolled her eyes.

18
00:01:02.253 --> 00:01:05.714
"You can't run on Saturn's rings, Jack.

19
00:01:06.374 --> 00:01:07.495
They're not solid.

20
00:01:08.055 --> 00:01:11.756
They're made of chunks of ice and rock that float around the planet."

21
00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:14.437
Terrell looked over from his computer.

22
00:01:14.457 --> 00:01:16.998
"I'm researching the first moon landing.

23
00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:19.539
You could definitely run on the moon.

24
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.920
You'd need a spacesuit though."

25
00:01:22.861 --> 00:01:23.541
Roxy nodded.

26
00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:26.442
"Plus, there isn't much gravity on the moon.

27
00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:28.803
So you could jump really high."

28
00:01:30.004 --> 00:01:30.684
Jack stood up.

29
00:01:31.368 --> 00:01:33.049
"Earth, this is Astronaut Jack.

30
00:01:33.769 --> 00:01:35.209
I just landed on the moon.

31
00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.510
I'm going to try moon jumping now!"

32
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.010
Jack jumped as high as he could.

33
00:01:40.591 --> 00:01:42.171
Roxy, Mara, and Terrell laughed.

34
00:01:45.092 --> 00:01:46.252
Miss Apricot walked over.

35
00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:50.633
"Jack, did you pick a topic for your project yet?"

36
00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:52.634
Jack scratched his head.

37
00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:55.134
"Uh, I might research aliens."

38
00:01:56.075 --> 00:01:57.255
Miss Apricot sighed.

39
00:01:57.815 --> 00:02:00.936
"Please pick something more serious than that.

40
00:02:02.384 --> 00:02:04.346
And stop jumping."

41
00:02:04.366 --> 00:02:06.207
"Okay, Miss Apricot."

42
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:07.608
Jack sat back down.

43
00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:10.330
"What are you writing about, Roxy?"

44
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:11.330
Terrell asked.

45
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.812
"Well," Roxy said.

46
00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:15.733
"I picked the planet Mercury.

47
00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:17.615
But it's not very interesting."

48
00:02:18.716 --> 00:02:20.317
Terrell looked thoughtful for a moment.

49
00:02:21.357 --> 00:02:24.239
"I have an idea—Rocket Girl."

50
00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.661
Roxy tried not to laugh.

51
00:02:27.281 --> 00:02:28.382
She knew Terrell was kidding.

52
00:02:28.402 --> 00:02:30.584
"Very funny, Terrell.

53
00:02:30.956 --> 00:02:34.078
But Rocket Girl has more important things to do than help me."

54
00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:36.059
Terrell shook his head.

55
00:02:36.079 --> 00:02:39.581
"No, I meant you should write about Rocket Girl.

56
00:02:40.362 --> 00:02:42.023
She can fly through space, right?

57
00:02:42.723 --> 00:02:46.165
And she's probably as fast as a comet."

58
00:02:46.185 --> 00:02:46.866
Mara chuckled.

59
00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:50.048
"That's ridiculous, Terrell!"

60
00:02:50.068 --> 00:02:53.290
"It's even sillier than my alien idea!"

61
00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:54.190
Jack said.

62
00:02:55.291 --> 00:02:56.892
Just then Roxy's watch beeped.

63
00:02:59.396 --> 00:03:01.578
"I'll be right back," she whispered to Terrell.

64
00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:03.400
"Mayor Bloom is calling me."

65
00:03:04.841 --> 00:03:06.483
Roxy stepped out of the computer center.

66
00:03:06.503 --> 00:03:08.865
"Mayor Bloom, what's wrong?"

67
00:03:08.885 --> 00:03:11.648
"I need your help, Rocket Girl!"

68
00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:12.669
Mayor Bloom said.

69
00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:15.912
"Metro City Central Bank was just robbed."

70
00:03:15.932 --> 00:03:18.754
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

71
00:03:18.774 --> 00:03:20.656
"I'll be there right away!"
